WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.900
Before the first sketch, there is always a question.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.800
What is this part for? You already know.

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.800
But you must repeat it. To the modeller, the solver, the drawing. Every time.

4
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.400
What if you only had to say it once?

5
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.900
DesignWizard.ai: the tool that remembers why.

6
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.700
Here, you do not start by drawing. You let the part speak.

7
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.000
I bolt on here. I take a shaft. I let a cable through.

8
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.700
And the tool proposes a shape, a stock size, and the steps to make it.

9
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:45.200
Then you tune it. A dimension climbs, and the housing stretches as you watch.

10
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.800
A wall too thin? A hole no standard drill can make?

11
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.700
The tool sees it before the shop does, and offers the fix.

12
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:01.400
And when you need several? A longer one. Another, without its window.

13
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.600
The same part, under another name. Its drawings, files and order follow.

14
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.600
No part lives alone. Each one already knows where it attaches.

15
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.200
Bring them together: they find their place, with no one showing them.

16
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.700
Change one, and the others follow. If two collide, you are told.

17
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.700
A product goes together by modules: each sets in as one block.

18
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:37.200
Electronics do not live elsewhere. The board is designed in the same project as its housing.

19
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:43.200
And the day it goes to fabrication, its files are ready.

20
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:50.500
Will it run hot? Will it hold? First, a calculation you can redo in pencil.

21
00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:56.400
Then the simulation. When the two answers disagree, the tool says so.

22
00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:02.600
Between two live conductors, it measures the shortest path. Everywhere.

23
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:09.600
Meanwhile, the drawing has drawn itself. The part changes? So does the drawing.

24
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.000
At the review, everyone looks at the same part, in the same place.

25
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:20.600
And on ordering day, everything fits in a single package.

26
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.600
And artificial intelligence? Hand it the file, as you would a brilliant new hire.

27
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.600
It proposes. You read. And nothing changes without your say-so.

28
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:40.400
The code is open to all. And your work is never locked in.

29
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.200
A part begins with a question.

30
00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:49.700
Here is the tool that remembers the answer: DesignWizard.ai.
